cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this project or its findings, please cite it as below."
title: "Silicon Entropy Engine — a CPU-native LLM co-designed for the memory wall"
abstract: >-
  A research project building a large, agentic-capable language model made fast on
  consumer CPUs (Ryzen 5 3600X / Zen 2, AVX2, no AVX-512 / VNNI) through architectural
  co-design: a cache-resident ternary, sparse SSM "thinking" core plus a sparse retrieval
  and mixture-of-experts "knowing" tier, sized to the L3 cache and validated end-to-end
  on real hardware.
authors:
  # Replace with given-names / family-names for a formal citation if you prefer.
  - name: "WildPino"
